## Problems and coverage

<IncidentReview />

## Shared parser: reads month before day

For day-first tenants, the shared parser interprets a date in month-first order. The classifier
assigns app/email reports and booking-v2 form reports to this group. Report `R-41200` says a
7 April reminder went out for 4 July. Verify this path against the tenant's date contract and
preserve the intended calendar date through parsing and serialization.

This grouping is based on tenant configuration and intake path. The timing reports above
remain a named exception requiring investigation; their inclusion is not proof of this root cause.

## Booking-v3 form: hint and parser disagree

The form displays `MM/DD/YYYY`, while its date reading follows the tenant's day-first order.
The affected form reports come from Alder Physio, Copper Studio and Pale Harbour.
Report `R-41230` describes 6 January becoming 1 June, although intake tagged it as a parser report.
Align the visible hint and accepted input format, then verify that entering the intended date
produces that date in storage and the invite.

## What the current component computes

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

